From 00452a025974825d3adfaba9e29eaa225ab7e27c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:24:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 233/270] tegra_dc: a display driver and accelerant for the
 NVIDIA Tegra 2

A first driver for the display controller of the Tegra 2 (Tegra20), as in
the Toshiba AC100. It keeps what the firmware set up (clocks, pins, panel
timing, window A scanning out of the memory it reserved) and offers the
panel at 32 as well as 16 bits per pixel, changing only the pixel format
and line stride of window A through its shadowed registers. The vertical
blank interrupt releases the retrace semaphore.

The scanout memory is mapped write combining as device memory, so that
the clone in app_server gets the same memory type. The driver only
publishes its device when it finds the display as expected; otherwise
app_server keeps using the frame buffer driver.

Register descriptions come from the Tegra 2 Technical Reference Manual,
chapter 29.

Signed-off-by: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
